From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS host apps in App Management

Settings > Apps > Manage your apps lists Linux apps installed on the
device itself, with a page of their own (nickel_detail_view): pin to
shelf, and the details block: "Linux app, installed with Flatpak |
Portage | AppImage" (from the package id nickel-appd gives the app), its
version, app size and data size. Uninstall is in the page's header (0015).
The OS image's own Linux apps (no package id) show as system apps.

When the page shows an app, App Management asks the publisher for its
size (UpdateAppSize); NickelHostApps asks nickel-appd
(org.nickelos.Apps.GetAppDetails), which reads them from what installed
the app, and publishes version and sizes.

Strings: "Linux app", "Linux app, installed with <installer>". The page's
per-type switches gain kNickelHost (metrics counted with Borealis's).

